  "articleBody": "It's a bummer when your tiny home doesn't live up to its spacious potential, and often, it comes down to how the initial planning happened. A common misstep is trying to cram a traditional home's layout into a smaller footprint instead of embracing a true small-space-first design approach. This often leads to awkward traffic flows, insufficient storage, and areas that just don't feel right. Another issue might be overlooking multi-functional elements or failing to plan for vertical space, leaving you with less usable room than you anticipated. Sometimes, it's also about not fully assessing your personal lifestyle needs at the outset – if the design wasn't built around *your* daily routines, it's bound to feel off. Zen Tiny Homes has spent over a decade perfecting the art of intentional small-space living, focusing on how you actually live, cook, and relax. We partner with clients from the very first property assessment through custom design to avoid these pitfalls, ensuring every square foot is optimized for functionality and comfort. If you're feeling restricted in your current tiny home or want to ensure your new build avoids these issues, it's definitely worth talking to experts who specialize in creating homes that use space intelligently. We can help identify what's making your space feel small and explore solutions to make it work better for you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-03"
